TA-baseline
====

Collects a host security baseline from the kernel/filesystem: UEFI SecureBoot state, kernel lockdown mode, SSH root-login and password-auth settings (sshd_config, including sshd.d), password aging policy (/etc/shadow), and auditd service state. Emits JSON events to index=main (sourcetype baseline:status) and baseline.* metrics to index=metrics (sourcetype baseline:metrics) hourly, with dashboards.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * none - systemd + standard files only
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="baseline:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="baseline:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="baseline.*" by host
  | mstats avg("baseline.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=baseline:status  (secure_boot, lockdown, sshd settings, aging, auditd)
Metrics: baseline.secure_boot, baseline.lockdown, baseline.auditd_active, baseline.weak_ssh,
         baseline.shadow_min_age, baseline.shadow_max_age
Dashboards: TA-Baseline > Baseline Overview / Baseline Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-baseline/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * SecureBoot reads the UEFI SecureBoot efivar (sudo -n cat fallback, explicit
    null marker when unreadable/BIOS); the efivar must be readable by the
    splunk user or sudoers must allow NOPASSWD /bin/cat of that path.
  * sshd_config.d drop-ins must be readable by the splunk user (file ACL plus
    execute/traverse ACL on the directory).
  * shadow file must be readable by splunkd (add splunk to group shadow).

License
-------
SOURCE-AVAILABLE (see LICENSE) - free personal, educational and evaluation
use; commercial or production use requires a paid license from BentleyPC
LLC (https://www.bentleypc.com/TA-baseline).

Enter your key (format BP-...) after purchase using EITHER method:

  1. Splunk Web: open the app, click "License" in the nav, click a row to
     open the key entry page, paste the key and Save.

  2. File (headless / forwarder friendly): create the file
     $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-baseline/local/license.conf with:

         [settings]
         telemetry_enabled = 1
         key = BP-xxxxxxxxxxxx

     No restart required - the hourly beacon reads this file on every run.

Set telemetry_enabled = 0 to keep the key for validation but pause all
outbound beacons. The beacon sends only: license key, hostname, app name
and app version to the BentleyPC license API (see api_base in
default/license.conf). It is telemetry only - never a license check that
blocks functionality.
